    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine is anchored today by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (84.88) and **Gunnar Henderson** (81.75), our two highest-scoring options. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Kay (xERA 4.67), where his dynamic platoon edge and favorable spot in the two-hole position propel him to the top of our lineup. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** faces a softer target in Lambert (xERA 4.28); his elite efficiency is bolstered significantly by his position as the leadoff hitter, maximizing his opportunities to contribute across our core categories. We are also banking on **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) to sustain his momentum, as he pairs a strong individual projection with a high-floor matchup against Lugo, despite the subtle drag caused by high-percentage hold catchers reducing his stolen base ceiling.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Miguel Vargas** on the bench with a score of 42.63. While his xwOBA of 0.401 is arguably the most impressive metric in our utility pool, he fell just short of the efficiency required to unseat **Curtis Mead** or **Nasim Nunez** in today\u2019s specific platoon-adjusted landscape. **Nasim Nunez** (50.33) remains a critical inclusion, as his elite speed is essential for our pursuit of the stolen base category, even in a lower-order spot against the lefty Jump. Meanwhile, we are monitoring the 30% rain risk hovering over the contest involving **Drake Baldwin** (71.33) and **Dominic Smith** (59.85); while both currently project as strong starts due to Quantrill\u2019s high xERA, their status remains contingent on the weather holding, and we are prepared to pivot to the bench should the rain risk escalate into a delay or cancellation.",
